# Cloudflare Pages headers (ADR-0008). Copied verbatim from public/ into the
# build root, where Cloudflare serves it. These headers make the deployed site
# cross-origin isolated, which is what backs `SharedArrayBuffer` and therefore
# the Slice 7 WASM thread pool (ADR-0007).
#
# This file is load-bearing for the Slice 8 service worker: Workbox precaches
# the *full network response* (headers included) at install time, so as long as
# every network response carries COOP/COEP, the SW-served cached index.html and
# .wasm stay cross-origin isolated offline. Drop these headers and the SW would
# serve a document without isolation → no SharedArrayBuffer → the render worker
# throws at boot → multicore silently off. The pwa-config guard test fails if
# COOP/COEP ever go missing here.
#
# Every asset is same-origin (self-hosted since Slice 0, watch-list #1), so
# COEP: require-corp has no cross-origin subresource to reject; CORP is added
# belt-and-braces.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
